{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
As I walked out one [D]morning fair,[A]
to view the fields and taste the air,[D]
for to view the fields and nettles around,[A]
I thought I heard some lonesome sound.[D]
I thought I heard my true love say,[A]
oh do turn and come this way.[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[D] [A] [A7] [D] [D] [A] [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You love some other, you [D]don’t love me,[A]
you care not for my company.[D]
You love some other and I know why,[A]
because he has more gold than I.[D]
But gold will melt and silver will fly,[A]
my love for you will never die.[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[D] [A] [A7] [D] [D] [A] [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
There is a flower I’ve [D]heard them say[A]
that can be seen from day to day,[D]
and if that flower I only could find[A]
to cure this aching heart of mine.[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[D] [A] [A7] [D] [D] [A] [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
So fare you well my [D]charming little love,[A]
oh meet me in that land above.[D]
And when we meet there in that land,[A]
we’ll take no more this parting hand.[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[D] [A] [A7] [D] [D] [A] [D]
{end_of_verse}
